If your application does not have endpoints like `/healthz` and `/ready`, you can still configure liveness and readiness probes using other types of checks. Kubernetes supports several types of probes, including HTTP GET, TCP socket, and exec commands.

### Example Using Exec Command Probes

If your application does not expose HTTP endpoints, you can use an `exec` command to check the health of the application. Here's how you can modify your pod configuration to include `exec` probes:

```python
import os
from kubernetes import client, config

