### Example Implementation with Prometheus and Grafana

Here's an example of how you can instrument your Jenkins pipeline to measure and report latencies in real-time using Prometheus and Grafana:

#### 1. Install Prometheus and Grafana

First, set up Prometheus and Grafana in your environment. You can install them using Docker or directly on your servers.

```sh
docker run -d --name prometheus -p 9090:9090 prom/prometheus
docker run -d --name grafana -p 3000:3000 grafana/grafana
```

#### 2. Instrument Your Jenkins Pipeline

Modify your Jenkins pipeline to measure and report latencies to Prometheus.

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any

    environment {
        PROMETHEUS_URL = 'http://localhost:9090'
        VAULT_ADDR = 'https://my-vault-instance.com'
        VAULT_TOKEN = 'my-vault-token'
    }

    stages {
        stage('Retrieve Secrets') {
            steps {
                script {
                    def startTime = System.currentTimeMillis()

                    def vaultClient = new com.hashicorp.hvac.Vault(VAULT_ADDR)
                    vaultClient.auth.token.login(VAULT_TOKEN)

                    def authLatency = System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime
                    reportLatency('auth_latency', authLatency)

                    startTime = System.currentTimeMillis()

                    // Retrieve secrets
                    def secret = vaultClient.secrets.kv.v2.readSecretVersion(path: 'secret/my-app/db-credentials')
                    def dbUsername = secret.data.data.username
                    def dbPassword = secret.data.data.password

                    def secretRetrievalLatency = System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime
                    reportLatency('secret_retrieval_latency', secretRetrievalLatency)

