spring.datasource.password=_prod_password
```

### Step 2: Configure Data Source Based on Environment

Create a configuration class to define the data source based on the active profile. You can use Spring profiles to manage different environments.

#### Example of `EnvironmentConfig.java`:
```java
@Configuration
@Profile({"dev", "staging", "prod"})
public class EnvironmentConfig {

    @Value("${spring.datasource.url}")
    private String dbUrl;

    @Value("${spring.datasource.username}")
    private String dbUsername;

    @Value("${spring.datasource.password}")
    private String dbPassword;

